<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Notification small icon — the brand's "flow / merge" glyph.

  Android renders the small (status bar) icon as a monochrome silhouette,
  so this is a single white stroked path on a transparent canvas. The art
  is the current brand mark (public/branding/logo-source.png): one long
  rounded bar from top-right to bottom-left, joined by a second rounded
  bar coming in from the top-left. Coordinates are the 1024px master
  remapped to the 24dp viewport; stroke width is the logo's own bar
  thickness (~136/1024) with round line caps, matching the source.

  The web-push twin of this glyph is the alpha-silhouette badge
  public/icons/badge-96x96.png (regenerated by scripts/generate-icons.cjs),
  so native and web notifications show the same mark.

  Referenced by:
    • api/_lib/fcm.ts              (android.notification.icon, FCM background)
    • src/utils/capacitorBridge.ts (LocalNotifications smallIcon)
    • AndroidManifest.xml          (default_notification_icon meta-data)

  The resource NAME (ic_stat_eduvora) is intentionally kept even though
  the artwork is the new brand: the FCM server sends this literal string
  with every push, so renaming it would make every already-installed app
  fail to resolve the drawable and fall back to an anonymous white box
  until those apps update. Replace the art freely; rename only after a
  full forced upgrade.

  Vector drawables are supported natively at minSdk 23, so a single file
  covers every density bucket.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="24dp"
    android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportWidth="24"
    android:viewportHeight="24">
    <path
        android:fillColor="#00000000"
        android:strokeColor="#FFFFFFFF"
        android:strokeWidth="3.19"
        android:strokeLineCap="round"
        android:pathData="M20.41,3.59 L3.23,20.77 M3.23,3.59 L11.82,12.18" />
</vector>
